# Data Model — Onchain Identity

## Entities

### Entity: Profile

A user's onchain identity. Stores name, avatar, bio, and verified links.

```yaml
entity: Profile
type: contract
properties:
  address:
    type: string
    format: address
    required: true
  name:
    type: string
    required: true
  avatar:
    type: string
    required: false
  bio:
    type: string
    required: false
  links:
    type: json
    required: false
  owner:
    type: string
    format: address
    required: true
states: [created, active, suspended]
lifecycle: created → active → suspended
```

### Entity: Registry

ENS-compatible registry mapping names to profile addresses.

```yaml
entity: Registry
type: contract
properties:
  address:
    type: string
    format: address
    required: true
  owner:
    type: string
    format: address
    required: true
states: [deployed, active]
lifecycle: deployed → active
```

### Entity: Resolver

ENS resolver that returns profile metadata for a given name.

```yaml
entity: Resolver
type: contract
properties:
  address:
    type: string
    format: address
    required: true
states: [deployed, active]
lifecycle: deployed → active
```

### Entity: Registrar

Subdomain registrar for base.eth. Users register `name.base.eth` subdomains.

```yaml
entity: Registrar
type: contract
properties:
  address:
    type: string
    format: address
    required: true
  parentDomain:
    type: string
    required: true
  registrationFee:
    type: number
    required: true
states: [deployed, active]
lifecycle: deployed → active
```

### Entity: Registration

A name registration event on the Base blockchain.

```yaml
entity: Registration
type: event
properties:
  name:
    type: string
    required: true
  owner:
    type: string
    format: address
    required: true
  profile:
    type: string
    format: address
    required: true
  timestamp:
    type: number
    required: true
states: [pending, confirmed]
lifecycle: pending → confirmed
```

## Relationships

### Relationship: Registrar → Profile

```yaml
relationship: Registrar -> Profile
verb: creates
cardinality: 1:1
required: true
description: Registering a name creates a profile
```

### Relationship: Registry → Profile

```yaml
relationship: Registry -> Profile
verb: maps
cardinality: 1:N
required: true
description: Registry maps ENS names to profile addresses
```

### Relationship: Resolver → Profile

```yaml
relationship: Resolver -> Profile
verb: resolves
cardinality: 1:N
required: true
description: Resolver returns profile metadata for ENS lookups
```

### Relationship: Profile → Base

```yaml
relationship: Profile -> Base
verb: deployed_on
cardinality: 1:1
required: true
description: All contracts deployed on Base Sepolia L2
```
